<article class="env-remark" id="05C7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05C7">Remark <span data-tag="05C7">10.66.12</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $M$ be an $S$-module. Denote $f : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ the associated map on spectra. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f(\text{Ass}_ S(M)) \subset \text{Ass}_ R(M) \subset \text{WeakAss}_ R(M) \subset f(\text{WeakAss}_ S(M))  \]
</div>
  <p> see Lemmas <a href="/tag/05BW" data-tag="05BW">10.63.11</a>, <a href="/tag/05C6" data-tag="05C6">10.66.11</a>, and <a href="/tag/0589" data-tag="0589">10.66.6</a>. In general all of the inclusions may be strict, see Remarks <a href="/tag/05BX" data-tag="05BX">10.63.12</a> and <a href="/tag/05C5" data-tag="05C5">10.66.10</a>. If $S$ is Noetherian, then all the inclusions are equalities as the outer two are equal by Lemma <a href="/tag/058A" data-tag="058A">10.66.9</a>. </p>
</article>